  "notes": "{安|やす}らぐ is an intransitive godan verb expressing a state of inner peace and tranquility.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive counterpart is {安|やす}らげる (to soothe, give comfort).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {心|こころ}が{安|やす}らぐ (one's heart feels at peace)\n- {気持|きも}ちが{安|やす}らぐ (to feel at ease)\n- {安|やす}らぎを{感|かん}じる (to feel peace/comfort)\n- {安|やす}らぎの{時間|じかん} (peaceful time)\n\nRELATED NOUN:\n{安|やす}らぎ is the nominalized form meaning \"peace, comfort, tranquility.\"\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {落|お}ち{着|つ}く: To calm down (from an agitated state)\n- リラックスする: To relax (more physical)\n- {安|やす}らぐ: Emphasizes inner peace and emotional comfort\n\nREGISTER: Neutral to slightly literary. Common in written contexts and poetic expressions.",
